# Vercel Web Analytics Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Next.js (App Router) project following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 using npm with `--legacy-peer-deps` flag
- Updated `package.json` to include the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with the new package and its dependencies

### 2. Code Integration
Modified `/web/src/app/layout.tsx`:
- Added import: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Added `<Analytics />` component to the layout's body, positioned before the existing `<SpeedInsights />` component

## Implementation Details

The implementation follows the Next.js App Router pattern as specified in the Vercel documentation:
- The Analytics component is imported from `@vercel/analytics/next` (framework-specific import for Next.js)
- Component is placed in the root layout file (`app/layout.tsx`) to ensure it's available across all pages
- Positioned alongside the existing SpeedInsights component for consistent monitoring setup

## Verification Steps Completed

1. ✅ **Build Verification**: Ran `npm run build` - Build completed successfully with no errors
2. ✅ **Linting**: Ran `npm run lint` - No linting errors introduced
3. ✅ **Testing**: Ran `npm run test` - All 4 tests passed
4. ✅ **Dependencies**: Package lock file updated correctly

## Notes

- The project already had `@vercel/speed-insights` configured, so the Analytics component was added alongside it
- Installation required `--legacy-peer-deps` flag due to peer dependency conflicts with the project's vite version (used in vitest)
- Once deployed to Vercel, you'll need to enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard under the Analytics section
- Analytics data will begin collecting automatically after deployment
- The Analytics component will track page views and visitor data following Vercel's privacy-compliant approach

## Next Steps for Deployment

1. Deploy the application to Vercel using `vercel deploy`
2. Navigate to the Vercel dashboard for your project
3. Click on "Analytics" in the sidebar
4. Click "Enable" to activate Web Analytics
5. Verify data collection by checking the Network tab for requests to `/_vercel/insights/*` after deployment
